.TH CHMAP_RESET 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chmap_reset \- clear all elements from the hash map
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chashmap.h>

ccol_retval_t chmap_reset(chmap chm, size_t new_bucket_array_size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Removes every key-value pair from the hash map, destroys all internal
data and, if asked, resizes the bucket/slot array. The map is usable
after the reset whether the resize succeeded or not.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
chm                      Hash map to reset
new_bucket_array_size    New bucket count (0 = keep current size;
                         values < 16 are raised to 16; otherwise
                         rounded up to the next power of two)
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success           - Every element was cleared (and the resize, if
                         asked for, succeeded)
ccol_not_enough_memory - The resize failed, but the elements are cleared
                         anyway
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
O(n) complexity, where n is the number of elements
Every element is destroyed whatever the return value is
Asserts if chm is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chmap_destroy (3),
.BR chmap_delete_elem (3)
